 "verdicts": {
  "GitHub's Spec Kit has four phases: Specify (user journeys and success criteria, not tech stack), Plan (stack, architecture, constraints), Tasks (small, independently implementable and testable chunks), and Implement; the developer verifies at each checkpoint before proceeding.": 1,
  "GitHub's stated rationale is that a vague prompt forces the model to guess thousands of unstated requirements, and claims specs give 'less guesswork, fewer surprises, and higher-quality code'; the post offers no quantitative evidence for this.": 1,
  "Spec Kit is installed with `uvx --from git+https://github.com/github/spec-kit.git specify init <PROJECT_NAME>` and driven by the /specify, /plan and /tasks commands, working with GitHub Copilot, Claude Code and Gemini CLI.": 1
 }
